{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGapOrder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGapOrder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NFCounitGapOrder.lean#L122-L125","doc":"The gap vanishes at `h = 0` (the classical point `q = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_dvd_h_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_dvd_h_sq","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NFCounitGapOrder.lean#L110-L120","doc":"**The consequence for the acceptance test.**  Any quantity of the form\n`h³ · c` vanishes to third order, so for the purposes of a Taylor comparison\npinned at first order and predicting second order, the gap is invisible:\nsubstituting `h = 0` kills it, as does its first and second derivative data.\nStated concretely as: the gap is a multiple of `h³`, hence of `h²`, hence of\n`h` — each of which is the algebraic content of \"contributes nothing below\norder three\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NFCounitGapOrder.lean#L104-L108","doc":"The gap at `h = 1` is exactly `3/2` — `1 − (−1/2)`, matching the closed\nform's cofactor `(1+2+2+2−1)/4 = 3/2`.  (Not `−1/4`: that is the cofactor's\nvalue at `h = 0`, a different quantity, and Lean caught the conflation.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.epsTyped_ne_epsSingleWrap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.epsTyped_ne_epsSingleWrap","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NFCounitGapOrder.lean#L97-L102","doc":"**The two counits are different**, so — `ε` being canonical, hence\nbasis-independent — the two NFs expand **different elements**.  Witnessed at\n`h = 1`, where the gap is `−1/4 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_cofactor_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_cofactor_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NFCounitGapOrder.lean#L90-L95","doc":"The cofactor at `h = 0` is `−1/4`: the leading term of the gap is `−h³/4`,\nso the vanishing is **exactly** to third order, not higher. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_eq_h_cubed_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_eq_h_cubed_mul","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NFCounitGapOrder.lean#L82-L88","doc":"**The gap is divisible by `h³`** — the two NFs agree through `O(h²)`.\nStated as an exact factorisation rather than an asymptotic claim, so it carries\nno analytic side conditions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.gap_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NFCounitGapOrder.lean#L71-L80","doc":"**The gap, in closed form.**  Reproduces the audit's `1.00579` at `q₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.epsTyped","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.epsTyped","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NFCounitGapOrder.lean#L65-L69","doc":"Counit of the same difference in the **typed 6-term** NF, the one the live\nmass compute uses:\n`ε(n−p) = h(h⁶+2h⁵+2h⁴+2h³−h²+2h−4)/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.epsSingleWrap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NFCounitGap.epsSingleWrap","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NFCounitGapOrder.lean#L59-L63","doc":"Counit of the neutron−proton difference in the **single-wrap** nucleon NF:\n`ε(n−p) = h(h−2)/2`.  (Recomputed symbolically in the companion probe and\nvalidated against the live `PROTON_NF`/`NEUTRON_NF`; it is the vector asserted\nin the 2026-06-16 counit-vs-trace audit.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}